---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title='Marcelo Ojeda | Software Architect · Integration · SaaS';
const description='Software Architect with 20+ years designing, integrating and evolving critical systems, enterprise platforms and SaaS products.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en">
<section class="hero"><span class="index">00 / PROFILE</span><div class="hero-meta">Santiago · Chile<br/>Architecture · Integration · SaaS</div><h1>I design systems<br/>that <em>evolve.</em></h1><div class="hero-copy"><p>Software Architect with 20+ years connecting business, software and operations — from enterprise platforms and omnichannel retail to SaaS products built from scratch.</p></div></section>
<div class="band"><div class="band-inner"><span>Architecture / Integration / Modernization / Product</span><span>Java · Spring · REST · GCP</span></div></div>
<section class="chapter" id="work"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">01 / Selected work</span><h2>Systems are understood through their decisions.</h2><p>Two architecture stories: different contexts, same principle — understand the operation before choosing the technology.</p></div><div class="story-list"><a class="story" href="/en/architecture/retail-omnichannel/"><span class="n">01</span><h3>B2B → omnichannel ecosystem</h3><p>Connecting stores, digital channels, ERP, WMS, inventory and logistics as one evolving operation.</p><span class="arrow">↗</span></a><a class="story" href="/en/architecture/saas-platform/"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Zero → multi-tenant SaaS</h3><p>Domain, security, APIs, web and cloud designed together as a product rather than independent parts.</p><span class="arrow">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="chapter evidence"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">02 / Evidence</span><h2>Architecture measured against real operations.</h2><p>The common thread is not a specific framework. It is taking responsibility for systems as business scale, channels and constraints change.</p></div><div class="evidence-grid"><article><b>~6×</b><span>inventory scale</span><p>Platforms supporting growth from roughly 800K to nearly 5M managed units.</p></article><article><b>50+</b><span>physical stores</span><p>Digital and physical channels connected with ERP, WMS, inventory and logistics.</p></article><article><b>0 → 1</b><span>SaaS product</span><p>Multi-tenant B2B product shaped from domain and security through cloud operation.</p></article><article><b>20+</b><span>years</span><p>Insurance, financial services, BI, retail, logistics, enterprise integration and SaaS.</p></article></div></section><section class="statement"><p>Architecture is not a diagram. <span>It is the set of decisions that lets a system survive change.</span></p></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">03 / Trajectory</span><h2>Two decades building systems that had to work.</h2></div><div class="timeline"><div class="timeline-row"><time>2011 — NOW</time><strong>Flores y Cía. S.A.</strong><p>Retail, logistics, omnichannel platforms, SAP Business One, WMS and enterprise integration.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>2024 — NOW</time><strong>Asymetrics</strong><p>Software Architect / co-founder. Multi-tenant B2B SaaS built from inception.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>2010</time><strong>BuilderHouse</strong><p>Technical leadership and Business Intelligence with IBM Cognos.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>2005 — 2010</time><strong>Cruz del Sur</strong><p>Digital insurance, online payments, WebSphere and financial integrations.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>2003 — 2005</time><strong>Soluziona</strong><p>Java / J2EE software engineering.</p></div></div><a class="pill-link" href="/en/about/">Full professional profile →</a></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">04 / Practice</span><h2>Hands-on enough to test the architecture.</h2><p>Technology is not the headline. It is how decisions become running systems.</p></div><div class="techline"><span>Software Architecture</span><span>Systems Integration</span><span>SaaS</span><span>Java</span><span>Spring Boot</span><span>REST APIs</span><span>React</span><span>SQL</span><span>Google Cloud</span></div></section>
<style>.evidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}.evidence-grid article{padding:2rem 1.5rem 2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.evidence-grid article+article{padding-left:1.5rem;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.evidence-grid b{display:block;font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,5rem);letter-spacing:-.06em;line-height:1;color:var(--accent)}.evidence-grid span{display:block;font:700 .65rem/1 monospace;text-transform:uppercase;margin:.7rem 0 1.4rem}.evidence-grid p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin:0}@media(max-width:760px){.evidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.evidence-grid article+article{border-left:0;padding-left:0}.evidence-grid article:nth-child(even){padding-left:1rem;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}}</style></BaseLayout>